aiproof (0.1.17) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New backend: the Claude Code CLI installed on this machine
    (provider "claude-cli", default model haiku). It uses the existing
    Claude subscription, so there is no API key to manage — the prompt goes
    in on stdin, the corrected text comes back on stdout. --strict-mcp-config
    skips loading the user's MCP servers, which measured ~2.7s of the CLI's
    ~5s startup; the call runs in a neutral cwd so no project CLAUDE.md is
    pulled into a proofread.
  * Eval on the 28-case suite: 27/28 passed with every case taking the
    first-attempt path (no repair or salvage calls), median 3.06s. Local
    qwen2.5:3b scores 23/28 at a median of 0.74s — so the CLI buys accuracy
    for latency, and makes a good fallback provider when Ollama is away.
  * Settings now states plainly whether the selected provider keeps text on
    this machine, and warns when the Claude CLI is not installed.

 -- Ed Watson <edmundwatson@gmail.com>  Tue, 13 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200

